Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Simone-Biles.md` (Enneagram Type 6, unpublished draft) against the entity-gap packet at `docs/content-analysis/entity-gaps/Simone-Biles.md`. Fresh-eyes notes are appended as a `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom of the draft. No body edits made.

**The two biggest issues:**

1. **Paris 2024 never happens in the body.** The draft goes twisties → rebuild → half-point spotter → Rabbit Hole → 2026 without ever showing her compete at the Games she rebuilt herself for. Three golds, the calf injury, the floor silver — the only reader-facing Paris beats are a passing clause and the Andrade bow buried in the Rabbit Hole. Beyond the factual hole, it leaves the thesis untested: the whole piece argues she can't accept a settled result, and Paris is the settled result she went back and got. The reader never learns whether it changed the answer.

2. **Jonathan Owens is furniture, not a relationship.** He appears three times ("love blanky," a Colts aside, a wing example) and "husband" is a top query on her name. The missing beat is the Dec 2023 Pivot podcast "I'm the catch" episode, the months of pile-on, and her Call Her Daddy response — which is the *same 2024 episode* the draft already mines for "Mom, come pick me up" and the driving analogy, so the source is in hand. It's also directly on-thesis: she cried over it, then defended the man being attacked.

Also flagged: the epigraph spends the Tokyo timeline's climax before the reader gets there; MBTI is a stated target keyword the page never answers; "Did I do it?" runs six times reader-facing; the ADHD/WADA paragraph is bolted onto the Nassar section with a bridge sentence it can't support. Preserved as working: the opening/closing bookend on air awareness, the three-year-old hallway scene, the procedural Tokyo timeline, the Kirk/Morgan concession, and the half-point spotter.

Sources: [NBC News — Biles on the backlash](https://www.nbcnews.com/pop-culture/pop-culture-news/simone-biles-says-backlash-husbands-viral-interview-really-hurt-rcna148379), [NBC News — Owens "unbothered"](https://www.nbcnews.com/pop-culture/pop-culture-news/simone-biles-husband-unbothered-interview-backlash-said-was-catch-marr-rcna131028)
